  "text": "Alternative Hypothesis Alternative Hypothesis In hypothesis testing, the null hypothesis and an alternative hypothesis are put forward. If the data are sufficiently strong to reject the null hypothesis, then the null hypothesis is rejected in favor of an alternative hypothesis. For instance, if the null hypothesis were that μ 1 = μ 2 then the alternative hypothesis (for a two-tailed test) would be μ1 ≠ μ2 .",
